{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778195531,"nonce":"+odenEJv+e+x2Rt6+P68pR/6ZW4=","message":"**New evidence (2026-05-07):** The path resolution is broken even for the MAIN worktree invocation, not just for worktrees.\n\nauth-merge.sh lives at `/Users/mll/Main/10 Projects/05 Utils/mandible/cli/auth-merge.sh`. Four levels up from `cli/` resolves to `/Users/mll/Main/`, so `dwt` is computed as `/Users/mll/Main/bin/dwt`. This path does not exist. The `[[ -x \"$dwt\" ]] || return 0` guard silently exits every time.\n\nThe bash-portability fix (dotfiles `39e2978`) fixed dwt being zsh-only, but the path bug (this issue) remained untouched and is now the active blocker.\n\nThree stale worktrees post-portability fix confirm this:\n- rlrmp: `feature__induced-gain-first-run` (auth `cab29866`)\n- rlrmp: `feature__feedbax-graph-step-adapter` (auth `99bb7f1c`)\n- feedbax: `feature__graph-public-step` (auth `5456e5be`)\n\n**Proposed fix:** replace the relative path with `command -v dwt` falling back to `${HOME}/.local/bin/dwt` (which exists as a symlink to `~/.dotfiles/bin/dwt`). Also: export `MANDIBLE_BIN_DIR` from `bin/mandible` is already done — derive `dwt` from `${MANDIBLE_BIN_DIR}/../bin/dwt` or rely on PATH.\n\nAlso see new duplicate issue `8dd6a9e` filed before I noticed this pre-existing issue.","files":null}]}